sketch-orca patch 0006: build OpenSSL 3.5.9 instead of OpenSSL 1.1.1w.
Modified for Sketch, 2026-11-01.

libslic3r includes openssl/md5.h (Utils.hpp, Format/bbs_3mf.cpp) and links OpenSSL::Crypto, so
the engine carries OpenSSL's libcrypto, statically. OpenSSL 1.1.1w, which Orca's recipe pins, is
under the OpenSSL and SSLeay licences, whose advertising clauses the FSF holds incompatible with
the GNU GPL family, the AGPL included. OpenSSL 3.0 and later are under the Apache License 2.0,
which is compatible with version 3 of the GPL and the AGPL. This patch pins OpenSSL 3.5.9, the
current release of the 3.5 long-term support series: the release archive from the OpenSSL
project's GitHub releases, with the SHA-256 the project publishes for it (also on openssl.org).
The configure options are upstream's. MD5_Init, MD5_Update and MD5_Final, which libslic3r
calls, are deprecated in OpenSSL 3 but still built (the configuration does not set
no-deprecated); the compiler warns about them and nothing else changes.

---
diff --git a/deps/OpenSSL/OpenSSL.cmake b/deps/OpenSSL/OpenSSL.cmake
--- a/deps/OpenSSL/OpenSSL.cmake
+++ b/deps/OpenSSL/OpenSSL.cmake
@@ -44,8 +44,10 @@ endif()
 
 ExternalProject_Add(dep_OpenSSL
     #EXCLUDE_FROM_ALL ON
-    URL "https://github.com/openssl/openssl/archive/OpenSSL_1_1_1w.tar.gz"
-    URL_HASH SHA256=2130E8C2FB3B79D1086186F78E59E8BC8D1A6AEDF17AB3907F4CB9AE20918C41
+    # Sketch (sketch-orca), 2026-11-01: OpenSSL 3.5.9 (the 3.5 long-term support release, under the Apache
+    # License 2.0) instead of 1.1.1w (under the OpenSSL and SSLeay licences); libslic3r uses it for MD5.
+    URL "https://github.com/openssl/openssl/releases/download/openssl-3.5.9/openssl-3.5.9.tar.gz"
+    URL_HASH SHA256=603f5602e2eef00d77fbd429d34dcd5822bb301757a1bc9cdb24c670f1eb859a
     # URL "https://github.com/openssl/openssl/archive/refs/tags/openssl-3.1.2.tar.gz"
     # URL_HASH SHA256=8c776993154652d0bb393f506d850b811517c8bd8d24b1008aef57fbe55d3f31
     DOWNLOAD_DIR ${DEP_DOWNLOAD_DIR}/OpenSSL
